'<!-- Exercises the #html, #markdown and #cpd parsing modes: raw HTML blocks, multi-line Markdown, mode nesting, inline conditions and macros. -->
#html
<style>
    .note {
        border-left: 3px solid #4a7;
        background: #f4f9f6;
        padding: 6px 10px;
        margin: 8px 0;
    }
    .note b { color: #275; }
    /* The "Markdown Elements - All" CSS snippet, which the report template omits.
       Tables go through thead/tbody so Calcpad's own tables are left alone. */
    blockquote {
        margin: 0.8em 0;
        padding: 2px 12px;
        border-left: 3px solid #99a;
        color: #445;
    }
    pre { background: #f6f6f6; border: 1pt solid #ddd; padding: 6px 10px; overflow-x: auto; }
    code { background: #f2f2f2; padding: 0 2px; }
    pre code { background: none; padding: 0; }
    table { border-collapse: collapse; margin: 1em 0; }
    thead th { background: #f0f0f0; border: 1pt solid #aaa; padding: 4px 8px; text-align: left; }
    tbody td { border: 1pt solid #ccc; padding: 4px 8px; }
    ul.contains-task-list { list-style: none; padding-left: 1.2em; }
    li.task-list-item input[type="checkbox"] { margin-right: 6px; }
    ins { text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: #4a7; }
    del { color: #888; }
    hr { border: 0; border-top: 1pt solid #ccc; margin: 1em 0; }
</style>
<div><span id="top"></span></div>
#end html
#markdown
# Parse Modes
A `#markdown` block renders **consecutive** lines together, so paragraphs,
tables and nested lists all work.

| Case | Load   | Factor |
|------|--------|--------|
| Dead | 5 kN   | 1.35   |
| Live | 3 kN   | 1.5    |
#cpd
#pre
#end cpd
- Ultimate limit state
  - 1.35 G + 1.5 Q
- Serviceability limit state
  - 1.0 G + 1.0 Q
#def test$ = Hello from macro
test$
#cpd
#show
#end cpd
Emphasis extras: ++inserted++, H~2~O, x^2^, ~~struck~~ and a bare URL
https://calcpad-ce.org — plus a task list:

- [x] Raw HTML passes through: <b>bold</b>
- [ ] Still to check
#end markdown
#cpd
"Inputs
G = 5kN
Q = 3kN
γ_G = 1.35
γ_Q = 1.5
"Design load
E_d = γ_G*G + γ_Q*Q
#html
<div class="note">
    <b>Note:</b> a <code>#cpd</code> block inside <code>#html</code> calculates,
    then <code>#end cpd</code> pops back to raw HTML.
#cpd
A = 2m*3m
q = E_d/A
#end cpd
</div>
#end html
#markdown E_d > 10kN
> The design load exceeds 10 kN, so this conditional Markdown block renders.
#end markdown
#markdown q > 100kPa
> Skipped: this condition is false, and these lines are never parsed as Calcpad.
#end markdown
#for i = 1:3
#html
<div class="note">Pass
#cpd
i
#end cpd
of 3 &mdash; the HTML block repeats once per iteration.</div>
#end html
#loop
#if E_d > 10kN
#html
<p class="note">Mode blocks nest inside <code>#if</code>.</p>
#end html
#else
#markdown
*Not taken.*
#end markdown
#end if
#def note$(text$) = <div class="note">text$</div>
#html
note$(Macros expand before parsing, so they work in every mode.)
#end html
#md on
'Contrast: `#md on` stays in Calcpad mode and renders **one comment line** at a time.
#md off
#markdown
Contrast: `#markdown` renders whole blocks, with no `'` quotes.
#end markdown
#markdown
## Styled Markdown

The `<style>` block at the top of this file is the **Markdown Elements - All**
CSS snippet, which covers what the report template leaves on browser defaults.

> A blockquote carries a left rule rather than a bare indent.

Fenced blocks keep the language on `code.language-*`, though nothing
highlights them:

```text
E_d = 1.35 G + 1.5 Q
A   = 2 m * 3 m
```

1. Ordered lists render alongside the bulleted ones above
2. Inline `code` keeps a background of its own

---

A rule separates sections without needing a heading.
#end markdown
#markdown
## Links

An `<img>` in an `#html` or `#markdown` block resolves `{project}` and
`{library}` the same way a `'` comment does.

A bare URL autolinks in `#markdown`: https://calcpad-ce.org — and so does
[an explicit Markdown link](https://github.com/imartincei/CalcpadCE).

Every link is confirmed before anything happens, because the target comes from
the worksheet.
#end markdown
#html
<div class="note">
    <b>http / https</b> — prompts with the URL, then opens in the browser:
    <a href="https://github.com/imartincei/CalcpadCE">CalcpadCE on GitHub</a>
    <br>
    <b>file</b> — prompts with the path, then opens with the system default.
    Must be absolute, so this one is machine-specific:
    <a href="file:///myfile.txt">Open file</a>
    <br>
    <b>Other schemes are ignored</b>, since the app uses URLs for navigation:
    <a href="mailto:someone@example.com">mailto</a>,
    <a href="javascript:alert('blocked')">javascript</a>
    <br>
    <b>In-document anchors</b> scroll within the preview: <a href="#top">back to the top</a>
    <br>
    <b>A quoted &gt; in an attribute</b> must not break the tag:
    <a href="https://example.com" title="Dead > Live">load comparison</a>
</div>
#end html
